{
  "total": 141,
  "totalPage": 3,
  "page": 3,
  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9f7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1995,
      "bookHadithIndex": 101,
      "text": "Ibn Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Do not argue with your brother, do not joke with him, and do not make a promise, only to not fulfill it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1995-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1995-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1995-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9f8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1996,
      "bookHadithIndex": 102,
      "text": "Aisha narrated:\"A man sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah while I was with him, so he said: 'What an evil son of his tribe, or brother of his tribe.' Then he admitted him and spoke with him. When he left, I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! You said what you said about him. Then you talked politely with him?' He said: 'O 'Aishah! Indeed among the evilest of people are those whom the people avoid, or who the people leave, fearing his filthy speech",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1996-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1996-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1996-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1996-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9f9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1997,
      "bookHadithIndex": 103,
      "text": "Muhammad bin Sirin narrated from Abu Hurairah - and I think he (narrated it from the Prophet) who said:\"Love your beloved moderately, perhaps he becomes hated to you someday. And hate whom you hate moderately, perhaps he becomes your beloved someday",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1997-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1997-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1997-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9fa",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1998,
      "bookHadithIndex": 104,
      "text": "Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Whoever has a mustard seed's weight of pride (arrogance) in his heart, shall not be admitted into Paradise. And whoever has a mustard seed's weight of faith in his heart, shall not be admitted into the Fire",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1998-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1998-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1998-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1998-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9fb",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 1999,
      "bookHadithIndex": 105,
      "text": "Abdullah narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever has a speck of pride (arrogance) in his heart, shall not be admitted into Paradise. And whoever has a speck of faith in his heart, shall not be admitted in to the Fire.'\" He said: \"So a man said to him: 'I like for my clothes to be nice, and my sandals to be nice?' So he said: 'Indeed Allah loves beauty. But pride is refusing the truth and belittling the people",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1999-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1999-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1999-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-1999-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9fc",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2000,
      "bookHadithIndex": 106,
      "text": "Iylas bin Salamah bin Al-Akwa' narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah said:\"A man shall remain exalting himself until he is written among the tyrants, so that he suffers from their afflictions",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2000-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2000-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2000-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9fd",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2001,
      "bookHadithIndex": 107,
      "text": "Jubair bin Mut'im narrated from his father who said:\"They (meaning the people in general) told me that I was proud, while I rode a donkey, wore a cloak, and I milked the sheep. And the Messenger of Allah said to me: \"Whoever does these, then there is no pride (arrogance) in him",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2001-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2001-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2001-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9fe",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2002,
      "bookHadithIndex": 108,
      "text": "Abu Ad-Dardh narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Nothing is heavier on the believer's Scale on the Day of Judgment than good character. For indeed Allah, Most High, is angered by the shameless obscene person",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2002-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2002-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2002-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2002-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0b9ff",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2003,
      "bookHadithIndex": 109,
      "text": "Abu Ad-Dardh narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Nothing is placed on the Scale that is heavier than good character. Indeed the person with good character will have attained the rank of the person of fasting and prayer",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2003-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2003-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2003-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba00",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2004,
      "bookHadithIndex": 110,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah was asked about that for which people are admitted into Paradise the most, so he said:\"Taqwa of Allah, and good character.\" And he was asked about that for which people are admitted into the Fire the most, and he said: \" The mouth and the private parts",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2004-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2004-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2004-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2004-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba01",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2005,
      "bookHadithIndex": 111,
      "text": "Abu Wahb narrated that :'Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak explained good character, and then he said: \"It is a smiling face, doing one's best in good, and refraining from harm",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2005-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba02",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2006,
      "bookHadithIndex": 112,
      "text": "Abu Al-Ahwas narrated from his father who said:\"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I stayed with a man who did not entertain me nor behave hospitably with me. Then he came to stay with me, shall I reciprocate the same to him?' He (ﷺ said: 'No, entertain him.\" He said: 'He (ﷺ saw me wearing tattered clothes and said:'(Do you have any wealth?' I said: 'Allah has given me various kinds of wealth through camels and goats.' He said: 'Then let it be seen on you)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2006-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2006-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2006-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2006-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba03",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2007,
      "bookHadithIndex": 113,
      "text": "Hudhaifah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“Do not be a people without a will of your own, saying: 'If people treat us well, we will treat them well; and if they do wrong, we will do wrong,' but accustom yourselves to do good if people do good, and do not behave unjustly if they do evil.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2007-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2007-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2007-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2007-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba04",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2008,
      "bookHadithIndex": 114,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Whoever visits the sick, or visits his brother in Allah (faith), a caller calls out: 'May you have goodness and livelihood be good, and may you dwell in an adobe in Paradise",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2008-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2008-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2008-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba05",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2009,
      "bookHadithIndex": 115,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Al-Haya is from faith, and faith is in Paradise. Obscenity is from rudeness, and rudeness is in the Fire",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2009-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2009-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2009-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2009-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba06",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2010,
      "bookHadithIndex": 116,
      "text": "Abdullah bin Sarjis Al-Muzam narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Taking the good route is a part of the twenty-four parts of Prophethood",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2010-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2010-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2010-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2010-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba07",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2011,
      "bookHadithIndex": 117,
      "text": "Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah said to the Ashajj 'Abdul-Qais:\"Indeed there are two traits in you that Allah loves: Forbearance, and deliberateness",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2011-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2011-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2011-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba08",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2012,
      "bookHadithIndex": 118,
      "text": "Abdullah-Muhaimin bin 'Abbas bin Sahl bin Sa'd As-Saidi narrated from his father, from his grandfather, who said that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Deliberateness is from Allah, and haste is from the Ash-shaitan",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2012-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2012-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2012-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2012-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba09",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2013,
      "bookHadithIndex": 119,
      "text": "Abu Ad-Darda narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Whoever was given his share of gentleness, then he has been given a share of good. And whoever has been prevented from his share of gentleness, then he has been prevented from his share of good",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2013-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2013-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2013-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2013-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba0a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2014,
      "bookHadithIndex": 120,
      "text": "Ibn 'Abbas narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah sent Mu'adh [bin Jabal] to Yemen, and said: 'Beware of the supplication of the oppressed; for indeed there is no barrier between it and Allah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2014-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2014-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2014-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2014-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba0b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2015,
      "bookHadithIndex": 121,
      "text": "Anas narrated:that \"I served the Prophet for ten years. He never said Uff and never blamed me by saying: 'Why did you do so' or why did you not do so?' And the Messenger Of Allah had the best character among all of the people. I never touched Khazz nor silk, nor anything softer than the hand of the Messenger of Allah, nor have I smelled musk, or a fragrance sweeter than the sweat of the Messenger of Allah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2015-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2015-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2015-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2015-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba0c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2016,
      "bookHadithIndex": 122,
      "text": "Abu Abdullah Al-Jadali narrated:\"I asked 'Aishah about the character of the Messenger of Allah. She said: 'He was not obscene, nor uttering obscenities, nor screaming in the markets, he would not return an evil with an evil, but rather he was pardoning and forgiving",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2016-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2016-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2016-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2016-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba0d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2017,
      "bookHadithIndex": 123,
      "text": "Aishah narrated:\"I was not jealous of any wife of the Prophet as I was jealous of Khadijah, and it was not because I saw her. It was only because the Messenger of Allah mentioned her so much, and because whenever he would slaughter a sheep, he would look for Khadijah's friends to gift them some of it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2017-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2017-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2017-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2017-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba0e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2018,
      "bookHadithIndex": 124,
      "text": "Jabir narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Indeed the most beloved among you to me, and the nearest to sit with me on the Day of Judgment is the best of you in character. And indeed, the most disliked among you to me, and the one sitting furthest from me on the Day of Judgement are the Thartharun, and the Mutashaddiqun and the Muthafaihiqun.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah! We know about the Thartharun, and the Mutashaddiqun, but what about the Muthafaihiqun?\"' He said:\"The arrogant",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2018-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2018-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2018-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2018-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba0f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2019,
      "bookHadithIndex": 125,
      "text": "Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"The believer is not one who curses others",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2019-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2019-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2019-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2019-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba10",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2020,
      "bookHadithIndex": 126,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that a man came to the Messenger of Allah and said:\"Teach me something that is not too much for me so that, perhaps, I may abide by it.\" He (S.A.W) said: \"Do not get angry.\" He repeated that (the request) a number of times, each time he replied: 'Do not get angry",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2020-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2020-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2020-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2020-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba11",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2021,
      "bookHadithIndex": 127,
      "text": "Sahl bim Mu'adh bin Anas Al-Juhani narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Whoever suppresses his rage while he is able to unleash it, Allah will call him before the heads (leaders) of creation on the Day of Judgement, so that he can inform Him of which of the Hur he would like",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2021-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2021-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba12",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2022,
      "bookHadithIndex": 128,
      "text": "Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"No young person honors an elder due to his age, except that Allah appoints for him one who will honor him at that age",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2022-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2022-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2022-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba13",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2023,
      "bookHadithIndex": 129,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.A.W) said:\"The gates of Paradise are opened on Monday and Thursday. In them, (will enter) whoever has not associated anything with Allah will be forgiven, except for the two who shun each other, (about whom) it is said: 'Return these two until they make amends",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2023-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2023-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2023-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2023-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba14",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2024,
      "bookHadithIndex": 130,
      "text": "Abu Sa'eed narrated:\"Some persons from the Ansar asked for (something) from the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) and he gave them. They again asked him for (something), and he gave them. Then he said: 'whatever of good that I have, I would never hoard it from any of you. (Remember) whoever abstains from asking others, Allah will make him content, and whoever tries to make due, Allah will suffice him. And whoever remains patient, Allah will make him patient. Nobody can be given a blessing better and more encompassing than patience",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2024-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2024-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2024-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2024-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba15",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2025,
      "bookHadithIndex": 131,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\"Indeed among the worst of people to Allah, on the Day of Judgment, is the two faced person",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2025-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2025-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2025-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2025-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba16",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2026,
      "bookHadithIndex": 132,
      "text": "Hammam bin Al-Harith said:\"Aman passed by Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman and it was said to him: \"This person conveys news about the people to the leaders.' So Hudaifah said: 'The Messenger of Allah said: 'The Qatat shall not enter paradise.'\" (Sahih)Sufyan said: \"The Qatat is the Nammam",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2026-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2026-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2026-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2026-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba17",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2027,
      "bookHadithIndex": 133,
      "text": "Abu Umamah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.A.W) said:\"Al-Haya' and Al-'Iy are two branches of faith, and Al-Badha and Al-Bayan are two branches of Hypocrisy",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2027-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2027-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2027-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba18",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2028,
      "bookHadithIndex": 134,
      "text": "Ibn 'Umar narrated that two men arrived during the time of the Messenger of Allah delivering an address. The people were amazed by their speech, so the Messenger of Allah turned to us and said:\"Indeed there is magic in eloquence'-or- 'Indeed some eloquence is magic",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2028-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2028-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2028-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2028-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba19",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2029,
      "bookHadithIndex": 135,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Charity does not diminish wealth, Allah does not increase a man in anything for his pardoning (others) but in honor, and none humbles himself for Allah but Allah raises him",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2029-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2029-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2029-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2029-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba1a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2030,
      "bookHadithIndex": 136,
      "text": "Ibn 'Umar narrated that Prophet said:\"Oppression shall be darkness on the Day of Judgment",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2030-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2030-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2030-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba1b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2031,
      "bookHadithIndex": 137,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) never criticized any food. if he liked it, he would eat it, and if not, he would leave it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2031-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2031-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2031-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2031-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c788dd1a4c9c86f0ba1c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 27,
      "hadithIndex": 2032,
      "bookHadithIndex": 138,
      "text": "Nafi' narrated that Ibn ‘Umar said:“The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) ascended the Minbar and called out with a raised voice: ’O you who accepted Islam with his tongue, while faith has not reached his heart! Do not harm the Muslims, nor revile them, nor spy on them to expose their secrets. For indeed whoever tries to expose his Muslims brother’s secrets, Allah exposes his secrets wide open, even if he were in the depth of his house.’” He (Nafl’) said: ‘ One day Ibn ‘Umar looked at the House- or – the Ka’bah and said: ‘What is it that is more honored than you, and whose honor is more sacred than yours! And the believer’s honor is more sacred to Allah than yours.’”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2032-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-27-2032-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
